@{SPL/1}

Drive a test-fix loop, but never loop forever and never touch the tests themselves.

$>
forbid 'Do not edit, skip or delete test files to make them pass'
forbid 'Do not run any command other than the test command'
let $cmd = 'npm test'

execute{command=$cmd} 'Run the test suite'

while{max=3, on_max='fail'} ?'the latest test output contains failures':
    think{level='medium'} 'Find the root cause of the failures in the latest test output'
    edit{target='production code'} 'Apply the smallest fix that resolves the root cause'
    execute{command=$cmd} 'Re-run the test suite'

out{len='two sentences'} 'Report that all tests pass and what was changed to get there.'
<$
